  "description": "Async pipeline runtime for .NET: resource-gated concurrency with adaptive/Bayesian tuning (and a pluggable custom-tuner hook, e.g. the always-learning EvalApp.Neural), sagas with compensation, middleware, pipelines that compose (a step can run another pipeline or itself; a context can hold pipelines, so outer loops drive inner pipelines), exclusive-resource guards that fail loudly or queue when two flows touch something non-thread-safe, a single-thread host mode (detected automatically on Blazor WebAssembly, one-core or CPU-pinned processes) that runs inline and yields cooperatively so a UI stays responsive, and a fluent builder. One entry point, one namespace: `using EvalApp;` then `Eval.App(...)...` â€” the whole public surface lives directly in the EvalApp namespace â€” no separate \"consumer\" namespace to learn. The shared runtime for Evaluated Applications products.",
